{"metadata": {"team_id": "uva", "run_id": "mq4cs-llamaft-splade", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "9-2_8", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "Great! To use your chain breaker tool, follow these steps:  1. **Position the Chain:** Slide the chain link you want to open in between the two prongs of the chain breaker tool. Ensure the prongs fit securely in the gaps on either side of the link.  2. **Align the Pin:** Turn the handle on your chain breaker tool clockwise so the small metal pin comes into contact with the chain link's pin.  3. **Disengage the Pin:** Continue turning the handle clockwise, which pushes the chain pin out of the rollers, allowing the chain to come apart.   4. **Detach the Chain:** Once the pin is pushed out, carefully stop turning the handle and lift your chain out of the tool.  5. **Separate the Link:** Grab the chain with your fingers on each side of the link and gently wiggle it back and forth until it separates.  6. **Remove the Tool Pin:** If needed, turn the handle counterclockwise to retract the chain tool's pin from the link.  Now your chain should be open. Remember to retain all parts, and avoid misplacing the pin if you plan to reuse it.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0020-78-15858:8": 1.0, "clueweb22-en0027-35-00252:2": 0.9597324427650187, "clueweb22-en0020-78-15858:3": 0.9578491421610098, "clueweb22-en0020-78-15858:11": 0.8848203053947581, "clueweb22-en0020-78-15858:7": 0.877029121777258, "clueweb22-en0020-78-15858:15": 0.8700500723982604, "clueweb22-en0031-00-17726:9": 0.8677764370303283, "clueweb22-en0020-78-15858:12": 0.8653586146783611, "clueweb22-en0027-35-00252:6": 0.8467984709453769, "clueweb22-en0010-59-02845:1": 0.8453608258256964}, "ptkb_provenance": ["I sometimes get overwhelmed by too many technical choices.", "I'm a casual bike rider.", "I have a small garage that I use as workshop space at home.", "I am not really handy with DIY."]}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0020-78-15858:8": 1.0, "clueweb22-en0027-35-00252:2": 0.