{"metadata": {"team_id": "uva", "run_id": "mq4cs-llamaft-splade", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "5-2_10", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "It's understandable to be concerned about your baby crying, but it's important to know that crying is a normal part of a newborn's communication. Babies cry for various reasons, such as needing a diaper change, being hungry, uncomfortable, or simply wanting comfort. While it can be challenging, remember that crying is their way of expressing needs.  There are many ways to soothe a crying baby. You can try holding your baby close, using gentle rocking motions, and providing comforting sounds like soft music or white noise. Swaddling can help them feel secure, and sometimes, a change in environment, like taking them for a stroll, might help calm them. Skin-to-skin contact and breastfeeding can also be soothing for many infants.  While it's impossible to prevent all crying, responding to your baby's needs with love and care will help them feel secure and reduce unnecessary distress. You'll quickly learn to understand what's making your baby cry and how best to comfort them. Remember, you\u2019re doing great, and it's okay to ask for help if you ever feel overwhelmed.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0028-51-09578:8": 7.320197068183779, "clueweb22-en0009-71-01981:11": 6.882503444108514, "clueweb22-en0029-92-05890:4": 6.753540377887688, "clueweb22-en0016-72-00066:5": 6.520877752246026, "clueweb22-en0009-71-01981:12": 6.109322466268303, "clueweb22-en0029-92-05890:5": 5.900268467093282, "clueweb22-en0041-37-00654:7": 5.623777033842893, "clueweb22-en0023-66-12715:1": 5.59558242394326, "clueweb22-en0046-77-00625:1": 5.5341720997058435, "clueweb22-en0008-36-00114:25": 5.117137755272981}, "ptkb_provenance": ["I am a woman."]}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0028-51-09578:8": 7.320197068183779, "clueweb22-en0009-71-01981:11": 6.882503444108514, "clueweb22-en0029-92-05890:4": 6.753540377887688, "clueweb22-en0016-72-00066:5": 6.520877752246