{"metadata": {"team_id": "uva", "run_id": "mq4cs-llamaft-splade", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "2-1_11", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "Roasting significantly affects the flavor, aroma, and acidity of coffee beans. During roasting, green coffee beans undergo chemical changes that produce the distinctive characteristics we associate with roasted coffee. The roast level\u2014ranging from light to dark\u2014has a powerful impact on the final taste of coffee.  Light roasts are typically brighter in acidity and showcase the original flavors of the coffee beans, including their fruity or floral notes. These roasts are often preferred by those who appreciate the bean's natural flavors. Medium roasts strike a balance between acidity and body, providing a more rounded flavor profile and often highlighting sweetness and chocolaty or nutty notes.  Dark roasts have a bolder, more robust flavor. The roasting process at this level reduces the acidity, making them smoother and easier on the stomach\u2014potentially beneficial if you experience mild acid reflux. Dark roasts develop pronounced bitter, smoky, or even chocolatey flavors, which might be appealing to those who enjoy a more intense coffee experience.  The roasting process can also influence the body of the coffee, with darker roasts typically yielding a heavier body. Given your preference for a less acidic coffee, you might enjoy trying a medium to dark roast for a smoother, fuller-bodied cup.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0035-10-05441:8": 1.0, "clueweb22-en0041-46-16463:4": 0.9772421743063254, "clueweb22-en0041-01-05927:8": 0.9524980766600188, "clueweb22-en0041-01-05927:9": 0.9486652193608368, "clueweb22-en0043-72-05460:6": 0.9478526375065931, "clueweb22-en0011-87-01475:6": 0.9315234687038305, "clueweb22-en0002-44-04650:1": 0.9192653096767519, "clueweb22-en0001-58-05338:9": 0.917240419040038, "clueweb22-en0018-85-19888:1": 0.9144540456615546, "clueweb22-en0043-98-11500:3": 0.9128937095367734}, "ptkb_provenan