like Robusta, Excelsa coffee has been regarded as poor quality, but this is more due to poor growing and processing practices than the bean itself. With the proper care, Excelsa has the potential to be specialty-grade coffee.", "Liberica beans make up only about 2% of the world's current coffee crop. Once upon a time, this varietal was far more critical after disease wiped out much of the world's Arabica supply. Arabica has since made a comeback, and Liberica production has primarily ceased. However, that may change in the future, as climate change makes it increasingly challenging to produce the more sensitive Arabica plants reliably. Liberica coffee has a unique flavor, pairing floral and fruity notes with a deep smokiness that some describe as woody. It has a full-bodied, reminiscent of Robusta coffee. It's not to everyone's taste, but there are some exceptional Liberica coffees to be had when done right."]}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0004-97-11464:6": 1.889622285704602, "clueweb22-en0036-21-16351:4": 1.5017451502656036, "clueweb22-en0031-16-17635:9": 1.4601309907604003, "clueweb22-en0004-97-11464:4": 1.4477043830766996, "clueweb22-en0004-97-11464:7": 1.4266367384775251, "clueweb22-en0036-21-16351:5": 1.4225717385485945, "clueweb22-en0035-25-05669:8": 1.4156799159495295, "clueweb22-en0031-16-17635:8": 1.4063402164936956, "clueweb22-en0022-85-00226:6": 1.249255480339869, "clueweb22-en0001-37-16016:10": 1.2394967327262605, "clueweb22-en0001-20-10010:19": 1.2119574063760636, "clueweb22-en0035-25-05669:12": 1.2066342315834555, "clueweb22-en0022-85-00226:7": 1.185384688627805, "clueweb22-en0035-25-05669:7": 1.1695768795249495, "clueweb22-en0019-88-13848:5": 1.168451938458265, "clueweb22-en0030-14-16395:14": 1.1460825847913976, "clueweb22-en0035-25-05669:9": 1.1386104044667746, "clueweb22-en0004-97-11464:3": 1.1235424409492303, "clueweb22-en0035-25-05669:13": 1.1118650976419973, "clueweb22-en0031-65-00073:17": 1.0895157243888516, "clueweb22-en0011-55-07210:14": 1.08