{"metadata": {"team_id": "uva", "run_id": "mq4cs-llamaft-splade", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "3-1_9", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "If you're not keen on taking supplements, taping can provide support during your recovery. The H-taping method is particularly effective for supporting injured finger pulleys. Here\u2019s how to apply it:  1. **Materials Needed**: Use rigid athletic tape, preferably 10cm long and 1.5cm wide.     2. **Prepare the Tape**: Cut the tape in half lengthwise from both ends, leaving a 1cm bridge in the middle.  3. **Positioning**: Flex your finger to approximately 60\u00b0 at the joint being taped. Place the tape so that the bridge is on the inside of the finger, aligned with the crease of the joint closest to the injured pulley.  4. **Applying the Tape**: Wrap the upper section of the tape around the finger, creating a ring. Do the same with the lower section below the joint. This setup helps maintain the tendon\u2019s proximity to the bone and limits finger flexion, essential for recovery.  5. **Retaping**: Since tape can stretch and lose effectiveness, retape between sessions to maintain support.  Remember, taping not only offers physical support but also serves as a psychological reminder of your injury.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:5": 1.0, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:4": 0.9779718808953622, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:9": 0.9761510140518602, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:10": 0.9523821294405652, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:12": 0.9439959854363787, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:13": 0.9108124941162868, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:2": 0.910056020937173, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:7": 0.9037143174801028, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:8": 0.8860621129581804, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:6": 0.8505626501326857}, "ptkb_provenance": ["I am climbing regularly for the past 3 years.", "I climb outdoors."]}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:5": 1.0, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:4": 0.9779718808953622, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727