{"metadata": {"team_id": "uva", "run_id": "mq4cs-llamaft-splade", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "5-2_2", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "Breastfeeding is not bad; in fact, it's highly beneficial for both you and your baby. It helps protect babies from infections, allergies, and certain illnesses, such as respiratory infections, gastroenteritis, and even reduces the risk of sudden infant death syndrome (SIDS). Breastfeeding can also promote better cognitive development in children and lower the risk of obesity and type 2 diabetes later in life.  For mothers, breastfeeding aids in burning extra calories, which can help you return to your pre-pregnancy weight more easily. It also reduces the risk of breast and ovarian cancers, type 2 diabetes, and osteoporosis. Moreover, breastfeeding can enhance the bond between you and your baby and may even reduce the likelihood of postpartum depression.  Breastfeeding is convenient as breast milk is always fresh, clean, and at the right temperature, sparing you the time and effort associated with formula feeding. However, if you have any dietary concerns, like calcium intake, it's a good idea to discuss with your healthcare provider to ensure you get proper nutrition while breastfeeding. Overall, breastfeeding is a great choice for your baby's health and your own well-being.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0020-42-17968:4": 3.302770380707568, "clueweb22-en0002-40-10883:4": 3.0058837161337575, "clueweb22-en0012-29-03517:7": 3.005768196543491, "clueweb22-en0011-87-07940:4": 2.917504389547994, "clueweb22-en0043-86-16051:3": 2.7083389206750037, "clueweb22-en0013-76-15640:15": 2.697440971357449, "clueweb22-en0027-55-05955:1": 2.6730359661163647, "clueweb22-en0009-37-07271:10": 2.6601774904722846, "clueweb22-en0040-60-11237:17": 2.4794298995905293, "clueweb22-en0000-85-06393:9": 2.4572562981311674}, "ptkb_provenance": ["I am a woman."]}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0020-42-17968:4": 3.302770380707568, "clueweb22-en0002-40-10883:4