{"metadata": {"team_id": "uva", "run_id": "mq4cs-llamaft-splade", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "8-1_9", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "Meetings interrupting your hyperfocus can be challenging, especially when you're in a productive groove. To manage this, try strategically scheduling your deep work sessions around your meetings to minimize disruption. If possible, plan to work on tasks that require intense concentration during blocks of time when you have no meetings scheduled.   Also, consider using a brief transition period between your focused work and meetings. This might involve taking a few minutes to mentally disengage from your task, jotting down where you left off, and what the next steps are, ensuring you can pick up smoothly afterward.   During meetings, keep a notepad handy to capture any thoughts about your current project. This practice can help ease the anxiety of stepping away from your work, as you'll have a record of your thoughts. After the meeting, allocate a few minutes to review your notes, which can help reacclimate you to your task.  Lastly, communicate with your colleagues about your productivity strategies. They may be willing to adjust meeting schedules or structures to support your workflow.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0041-12-03522:7": 1.0, "clueweb22-en0046-52-03977:16": 0.8770198381109041, "clueweb22-en0041-12-03522:5": 0.8724419264896828, "clueweb22-en0022-33-08001:9": 0.8709171297727684, "clueweb22-en0006-62-03234:3": 0.8555507488517232, "clueweb22-en0022-33-08001:8": 0.819957282702444, "clueweb22-en0004-49-00618:10": 0.7748805723609292, "clueweb22-en0014-73-14286:7": 0.7550052689399034, "clueweb22-en0019-85-03855:11": 0.7490872413989031, "clueweb22-en0034-02-04456:2": 0.745179980392094}, "ptkb_provenance": ["I work in an office.", "I have a sedentary lifestyle."]}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0041-12-03522:7": 1.0, "clueweb22-en0046-52-03977:16": 0.8770198381109041, "clueweb22-en0041-12-03522:5": 0.8724419264896828, "c