{"metadata": {"team_id": "uva", "run_id": "mq4cs-llamaft-splade", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "6-1_12", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "After microneedling, it's important to be cautious about the skincare products you use to ensure proper healing and avoid irritation. Salicylic acid, commonly found in face washes for oily skin, is a beta hydroxy acid (BHA) known for its ability to deeply cleanse pores and control oil. However, it's best to avoid using products containing salicylic acid immediately after microneedling, as it can be too harsh and potentially exacerbate skin sensitivity and irritation.  Instead, focus on gentle, hydrating products that promote healing. Hyaluronic acid is recommended for its hydrating and soothing properties. You should also temporarily stop using other strong exfoliating acids or retinol-based products. Generally, it's advisable to wait at least a few days or until your skin has calmed down before reintroducing salicylic acid into your routine.  As for your oily scalp and hair, you can continue your usual hair care routine unless advised otherwise by a professional, as treatments for your face and scalp are separate. However, be cautious not to let any hair care products run onto your face after microneedling, as this might irritate the freshly treated skin.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0009-89-01915:7": 4.1380489205289575, "clueweb22-en0023-06-19151:1": 4.09808606765853, "clueweb22-en0023-06-19151:2": 3.4036581057148245, "clueweb22-en0019-72-05705:11": 3.2844880452884757, "clueweb22-en0033-92-13251:6": 3.1840951492661493, "clueweb22-en0019-72-05705:10": 2.6808621772970804, "clueweb22-en0030-54-07790:7": 2.1164600724731923, "clueweb22-en0007-31-11995:8": 2.0660580243066518, "clueweb22-en0035-17-10361:9": 2.02197721407356, "clueweb22-en0009-89-01915:6": 2.0100028666381213}, "ptkb_provenance": ["I use AHA BHA serum once a week.", "I apply Hyaluronic Acid two times a day after washing my face."]}], "references": {"clueweb22-e