{"metadata": {"team_id": "uva", "run_id": "mq4cs-llamaft-splade", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "5-2_7", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "Breastfeeding is highly recommended for both infants and mothers due to its numerous health benefits. Breast milk provides optimal nutrition and has unique components that are beneficial for your baby's growth and immune system. It contains antibodies and enzymes that help protect your baby from infections and can reduce the risk of certain illnesses in infants. Additionally, breastfeeding benefits moms by aiding in postpartum recovery, promoting bonding with the baby, and reducing the risk of certain cancers and diseases.  Experts like the World Health Organization and other health bodies suggest exclusive breastfeeding for about the first six months of your baby's life. After this period, breastfeeding can be continued alongside the introduction of solid foods up to two years or longer if both you and your child wish. While there might be social or public misconceptions, medically speaking, breastfeeding is a healthy choice and not harmful. If you have any specific concerns or health conditions, it might be helpful to consult with a healthcare provider for personalized advice.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0011-87-07940:4": 6.219664949570002, "clueweb22-en0030-72-17249:1": 4.8519130432396365, "clueweb22-en0021-49-11932:5": 4.579300311499129, "clueweb22-en0012-29-03517:7": 4.204495973262748, "clueweb22-en0042-67-07776:2": 3.8591436150336516, "clueweb22-en0009-37-07271:10": 3.752897035642305, "clueweb22-en0013-14-15472:2": 3.729089483223827, "clueweb22-en0002-40-10883:4": 3.5625193790343803, "clueweb22-en0011-87-07940:2": 3.4961341570032487, "clueweb22-en0043-44-17412:15": 3.4365394866399486}, "ptkb_provenance": ["I think I don't get enough calcium, and I am worried about it.", "I am a woman."]}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0011-87-07940:4": 6.219664949570002, "clueweb22-en0030-72-17249:1": 4.8519130432396365, "clueweb22-