{"metadata": {"team_id": "uva", "run_id": "mq4cs-llamaft-splade", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "8-1_5", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "Using a timer to manage focus involves setting specific time blocks to concentrate on one task. A popular method is the Pomodoro Technique, which suggests breaking work into 25-minute intervals, known as \"pomodoros,\" followed by a 5-minute break. Here\u2019s how you can implement it:  1. **Pick a Task:** Choose a task to focus on. It can be helpful to pick one that is clearly defined and manageable within the time frame.  2. **Set the Timer:** Use a timer or an app to set a period, traditionally 25 minutes, though you can customize the duration based on your preference.   3. **Work on the Task:** Focus solely on the task during this period. Turn off potential distractions, like putting your phone on airplane mode.  4. **Take a Break:** When the timer rings, take a 5-minute break. Use this time to stretch, relax, or clear your mind.  5. **Repeat the Cycle:** After four cycles, consider taking a longer break of 15-30 minutes to recharge.  By setting a structure and using timed sessions, you create a sense of urgency and focus, which can help manage distractions and improve task completion.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0011-52-17888:2": 1.0, "clueweb22-en0025-68-10509:3": 0.8951318174191798, "clueweb22-en0023-24-19944:8": 0.8611420638827015, "clueweb22-en0001-30-00712:21": 0.8559904557257213, "clueweb22-en0023-24-19944:7": 0.8557238508245661, "clueweb22-en0029-26-09570:14": 0.8428459228567554, "clueweb22-en0023-48-06955:4": 0.83436428466316, "clueweb22-en0004-13-14479:5": 0.8332822513795392, "clueweb22-en0025-68-10509:7": 0.8220255082219209, "clueweb22-en0017-07-18143:6": 0.8091735852894417}, "ptkb_provenance": []}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0011-52-17888:2": 1.0, "clueweb22-en0025-68-10509:3": 0.8951318174191798, "clueweb22-en0023-24-19944:8": 0.8611420638827015, "clueweb22-en0001-30-00712:21": 0.8559904557257213, "clu