{"metadata": {"team_id": "uva", "run_id": "mq4cs-llamaft-splade", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "9-2_5", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "The jockey, also known as jockey wheels or jockey pulleys, are an essential part of your bike's derailleur system. They consist of two small guide pulleys located within a cage. The upper wheel, called the guide pulley, is closest to the sprockets and helps direct the chain as it shifts between gears. It often features more lateral play to assist in smooth transitions, even when the chain line isn't perfectly straight. The lower wheel is known as the tension pulley and its primary role is to maintain tension in the chain. Both pulleys work together to absorb slack in the chain and ensure the drivetrain operates smoothly. If you're adjusting your bike's chain or dealing with shifting issues, checking the jockey wheels for alignment and wear can be a helpful troubleshooting step.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0003-19-13577:3": 3.6236638597318622, "clueweb22-en0032-78-01787:0": 3.0, "clueweb22-en0008-56-06367:4": 2.9822742378372022, "clueweb22-en0040-35-09091:0": 2.760598497206905, "clueweb22-en0025-87-12863:0": 2.7568578945048805, "clueweb22-en0032-78-01787:1": 2.6148015057003833, "clueweb22-en0039-65-07416:1": 2.578222168017562, "clueweb22-en0039-65-07416:2": 2.558239901855946, "clueweb22-en0021-90-01123:2": 2.4955092420380094, "clueweb22-en0018-20-12295:0": 2.419844847896713}, "ptkb_provenance": ["I'm a casual bike rider.", "I take my bike in the train and the bus.", "I like biking even in rainy weather and in the forest."]}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0003-19-13577:3": 3.6236638597318622, "clueweb22-en0032-78-01787:0": 3.0, "clueweb22-en0008-56-06367:4": 2.9822742378372022, "clueweb22-en0040-35-09091:0": 2.760598497206905, "clueweb22-en0025-87-12863:0": 2.7568578945048805, "clueweb22-en0032-78-01787:1": 2.6148015057003833, "clueweb22-en0039-65-07416:1": 2.578222168017562, "clueweb22-en0039-65-07416:2": 2.558239901855946