{"metadata": {"team_id": "uva", "run_id": "mq4cs-llamaft-splade", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "3-1_10", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "The H-taping method is highly recommended for providing substantial support to pulley injuries. It's particularly effective in keeping the tendons close to the bone during activities like crimping, where your finger is flexed and under pressure. To perform H-taping, you\u2019ll need rigid athletic tape, ideally Leukoplast for its effectiveness. Start by cutting a 10 cm long and 1.5 cm wide strip of tape. Fold the strip in half lengthwise and cut a slit in the middle about halfway through the tape, creating an \"H\" shape. Place the center of the tape over the injured pulley area with your finger straight. Wrap the arms of the \"H\" around the finger, ensuring they overlap by about 50%. This method restricts finger motion, which is crucial for preventing further injury while climbing or performing daily activities. H-taping also serves as a useful physical and psychological reminder of your injury, aiding in your recovery process.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:4": 9.286473290224608, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:10": 9.22457656390772, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:5": 9.151632383549593, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:7": 9.130662505838286, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:2": 8.783291274781279, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:12": 8.7175653822811, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:6": 8.65007730792258, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:13": 8.183920101935813, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:1": 8.061107939822884, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:8": 7.902324156882888}, "ptkb_provenance": []}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:4": 9.286473290224608, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:10": 9.22457656390772, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:5": 9.151632383549593, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:7": 9.130662505838286, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:2": 8.783291274781279, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:12": 8.7175653822811, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:6": 8.65007730792258, "clu