{"metadata": {"team_id": "uva", "run_id": "mq4cs-llamaft-splade", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "9-1_7", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "To enhance comfort for your hands while riding, consider upgrading your handlebar setup. Since you're a casual mountain bike rider who values comfort over speed, and given your concern about back pain, choosing the right handlebars is crucial. Riser bars could be a good choice as they bring you into a more upright position, offering better control on steep and rough terrain. With riser bars, you'll find a natural increase in comfort and control, particularly on hilly or challenging trails.  Look for bars with an appropriate amount of rise, typically between 40-50mm, which could help relieve pressure on your wrists and shoulders, improving overall comfort. Also, check for a comfortable backsweep angle that suits your riding position to minimize strain on your wrists.  Considering your preference for upgrading over replacing, adding more ergonomic grips or bar ends can also increase comfort and control, distributing pressure more evenly across your hands and wrists. This can significantly enhance your riding experience on forest trails and rough paths.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0015-99-08241:0": 3.639699538351624, "clueweb22-en0015-99-08241:1": 3.4398753081989657, "clueweb22-en0015-99-08241:9": 3.3779095921577658, "clueweb22-en0038-73-02918:5": 3.090144029621552, "clueweb22-en0031-94-19558:2": 2.505789053163462, "clueweb22-en0001-50-03380:16": 2.5008361278534825, "clueweb22-en0012-64-00676:1": 2.4789622548379304, "clueweb22-en0031-94-19558:16": 2.4261750126059463, "clueweb22-en0031-94-19558:1": 2.4178348553967863, "clueweb22-en0023-62-08521:1": 2.3181894659697453}, "ptkb_provenance": ["I value comfort over speed.", "I am a casual bike rider.", "I recently moved to a city with more hills and rough paths.", "I like biking even in rainy weather and in the forest.", "I enjoy Mediterranean food."]}], "references": {"clueweb22